You don't need to be an advanced Python developer.

You should be comfortable with:

variables
strings
lists
dictionaries
if/else
for loops
functions
exceptions
classes/objects
modules
JSON


Especially understand dictionaries:

server = {
    "name": "web-server",
    "environment": "prod",
    "port": 443
}

print(server["name"])

Because AWS API requests and responses are heavily dictionary/JSON oriented.
